FloodWise is a community-powered flood awareness and navigation system designed for Marikina City.

It allows residents to view current flood conditions, report what they observe, check road and pedestrian passability, find evacuation shelters, receive location-based alerts, and get flood-aware route recommendations.

To improve reliability, community reports include timestamps, locations, verification statuses, and supporting information. Users are also reminded to report only what they genuinely observe and never put themselves in danger just to submit a report.

FloodWise also includes an AI assistant that helps users understand flood conditions and routes, while an LGU/DRRM dashboard allows authorized personnel to monitor reports, manage shelters, and provide official information.

The main goal is to connect community observations, technology, and local disaster management so people can make better-informed decisions during flooding.

